## Site-wide macros

Defined in `site/katex.config.ts` and available on every page.

| Macro | Renders | Meaning |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `\R` | $\R$ | real numbers |
| `\E` | $\E$ | expectation |
| `\T` | $\T_x\calM$ | tangent space (with `\calM`) |
| `\retr` | $\retr(x, v)$ | retraction |
| `\invretr` | $\invretr(x, y)$ | inverse retraction |
| `\transpose` | $A\transpose$ | transpose |
| `\defeq` | $a \defeq b$ | definition |
| `\bbX`, `\calX`, `\scrX`, `\bfX`, `\rmX` | $\bbR,\ \calI,\ \scrF,\ \bfA,\ \rmT$ | font shorthands for any letter |
| `\bfx`, `\rmx`, `\bfalpha` | $\bfx,\ \rmd,\ \bfalpha$ | lower-case and Greek variants |

## Conventions

- $x \oplus \delta = \retr(x, \delta)$: the point reached from $x$ along the tangent coordinates
  $\delta$. The retraction *defines* tangent coordinates
  ([Manifolds and retractions](../../concepts/manifolds/)).
- $x \ominus \mu = \invretr(\mu, x)$: the tangent vector from $\mu$ to $x$, so
  $(\mu \oplus \delta) \ominus \mu = \delta$. The mirror identity $\mu \ominus (\mu \oplus \delta) = -\delta$
  holds only on flat manifolds.
- $r = L^{-1}(x \ominus \mu)$: a whitened residual, with $\Sigma = LL\transpose$.
- $\calI(\theta)$: the (expected) Fisher information.
- $J$: a Jacobian with rows indexed by residual or argument coordinates and columns by free tangent
  coordinates.

## Page-local macros

A page defines its own notation in frontmatter, and those definitions override the site-wide ones on
that page only:

```yaml
katex_macros:
  \fisher: \mathcal{I}
  \params: \theta
```

The Markdown version of a page (`.md`) keeps this frontmatter, so its macros are always visible.
